{
  "$comment": [
    "Validation matrix. Every case is solved by BOTH the TypeScript engine and",
    "the Python reference solver, then compared.",
    "",
    "The spread is deliberate: it is not enough to check that two",
    "implementations agree on the default model. The interesting cases are the",
    "edges — one floor (Rayleigh damping can only hit one mode), twenty floors,",
    "a material override for damping, and all three ground-motion presets.",
    "",
    "Cases are checked into the repo rather than generated, so the validation is",
    "reproducible and a reviewer can see exactly what was compared."
  ],
  "cases": [
